# A hash table written in Ovis (generics.md §8): each key has a place found
# from its hash, or the next free one after it (open addressing). Its keys
# are any type that can be hashed and compared.
a hashable can:
    hash of (it) gives a whole number

a whole number is hashable:
    hash of (it):
        h = it mod 4294967296
        if h < 0:
            h = 0 - h
        give back (h * 40503) mod 4294967296

text is hashable:
    hash of (it):
        h = 5381
        for each i in the numbers from 1 to number of characters in it:
            c = character i of it
            h = (h * 33 + code of c) mod 4294967296
            free c
        give back h

a table from (key) to (value) has:
    keys (pointer to many keys)
    values (pointer to many values)
    used (pointer to many truth values)
    count (whole number, 0)
    room (whole number, 0)

# Where `k` is, or the free place where it would go.
to the place of (k: any hashable and equatable key) in (t: table from key to any value):
    at = (hash of k) mod room of t
    while the truth value at (used of t moved by at truth values):
        if the key at (keys of t moved by at keys) = k:
            give back at
        at = (at + 1) mod room of t
    give back at

to store (v: any value) under (k: any hashable and equatable key) in (t: table from key to value):
    if (count of t + 1) * 2 > room of t:
        make room in t
    at = the place of k in t
    if not the truth value at (used of t moved by at truth values):
        set the truth value at (used of t moved by at truth values) to true
        set the key at (keys of t moved by at keys) to k
        increase count of t by 1
    set the value at (values of t moved by at values) to v

# Twice the room, each key put in its new place.
to make room in (t: table from any hashable and equatable key to any value):
    old keys = keys of t
    old values = values of t
    old used = used of t
    old room = room of t
    room of t = old room * 2 + 8
    keys of t = new room for room of t keys
    values of t = new room for room of t values
    used of t = new room for room of t truth values
    count of t = 0
    for each i in the numbers from 0 to old room - 1:
        if the truth value at (old used moved by i truth values):
            store (the value at (old values moved by i values)) under (the key at (old keys moved by i keys)) in t
    free old keys
    free old values
    free old used

to (t: table from any hashable and equatable key to any value) holds (k: key):
    if room of t = 0:
        give back false
    give back the truth value at (used of t moved by (the place of k in t) truth values)

to the value under (k: any hashable and equatable key) in (t: table from key to any value):
    if not t holds k:
        show "The table holds nothing under this key."
        end the program
    give back the value at (values of t moved by (the place of k in t) values)
